  "offensiveAbilities": [
    {
      "name": "Breath Weapon",
      "actions": 2,
      "traits": [],
      "description": "<p>The zombie dragon breathes a wave of fetid viscera that deals <span class=\"roll\" onclick=\"roll(this)\">5d6</span> bludgeoning plus <span class=\"roll\" onclick=\"roll(this)\">5d6</span> poison damage (DC 28 basic Reflex save). A creature that critically fails is also Sickened 2.</p>\n<p>The zombie dragon can't use Breath Weapon again for <span class=\"roll\" onclick=\"roll(this)\">1d4</span> rounds.</p>",
      "collapsed": false
    }
  ],
  "spellcastingEntries": [],
  "description": "<p>The rotted husk of a once great dragon, this abomination has lost all its former splendor, but none of the ferocity. Its patchy, rotted wings don't generate enough lift to keep it aloft, but the foul necromantic energies animating it still allow it to fly, albeit slowly.</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Necromancers most often create these mindless undead as obedient, expendable servitors. Left to its own devices, a zombie seeks only to consume the living, stopping only when its rotting body can no longer hold together.</p>",
  "recallKnowledge": "Arcana, Religion, DC: 26",
